# iter-464 custom_frontend: "Autosave without asking" (docs/CUSTOM_FRONTEND.md 5.6). A player
# setting, DEFAULT ON (settings/mod_options.ini autosave_without_asking; the SETTINGS panel and
# the pause menu's MORE OPTIONS toggle it). The game's own save popup is answered with the
# game's own button (Save Game -> the current slot -> Yes / OK), so the game's own save code
# runs; the popups are never shown. With the setting OFF the game asks, as on a console.
#
# MAIN_HUD is loaded for the whole time the in-game save flow can run (the PromptInGameSave
# answer opens ITS save-slot picker, Main_Hud.ShowSaveSlots). Its class block (sprite 65)
# already uses 243 of 256 one-byte ConstantPool slots, so the code lives in the small
# BistroBaseScreen InitAction (sprite 64, runs first) and the Main_Hud functions only call
# _global.SRAutoSave.Hud(ev, this, arg) / Teardown (3 new pool names).
movie MAIN_HUD
append-to action initaction:BistroBaseScreen file=srautosave.aptasm
# HudLoaded: the HUD is ready (RegisterHudInstance); reg1 = this, reg2 = _global (0x129)
append-to function HudLoaded in Main_Hud
    op_76
    Push [reg1]
    EA_PushOne
    EA_PushByte 3
    Push [reg2]
    EA_GetNamedMember 'SRAutoSave'
    EA_CallNamedMethodPop 'Hud'
end
# ShowSaveSlots: a log line only. The hidden picker is prepared by the popup hook BEFORE the game
# calls ShowSaveSlots (PrepSlots, iter-465). In a Main_Hud function the C++ calls, a call into
# SRAutoSave (Hud) never ran (archive/v1_save/rolls/p1, p2) although _global.SRAutoSave and the
# disc's own pool names resolve there (probe, rolls/p3); inline GetURL works. So the C++-called
# Main_Hud functions only use inline strings.
prepend-to function ShowSaveSlots in Main_Hud
    GetURL 'FSCommand:SR_Log', 'hud ShowSaveSlots'
end
# SaveComplete(success r3) / LoadComplete(success r3): the host's current-slot tracker, with
# inline strings only (no pool lookup, see ShowSaveSlots). The autosave itself ends in the popup
# hook (SAVE SUCCESSFUL, k 3).
prepend-to function SaveComplete in Main_Hud
    Push [reg3]
    Not
    If hsc_done
    GetURL 'FSCommand:SR_SaveEvent', 'save'
hsc_done:
end
prepend-to function LoadComplete in Main_Hud
    Push [reg3]
    Not
    If hlc_done
    GetURL 'FSCommand:SR_SaveEvent', 'load'
hlc_done:
end
# ExitScreen: restore + delete the methods (Teardown deletes all but itself; it goes here,
# after it returned) - the lifetime rule of 10_menu.patch
prepend-to function ExitScreen in Main_Hud file=hud_exitscreen_head.aptasm

# The in-game SAVE/LOAD screen (pause menu): the same tracker events (no reply needed).
# ScrSaveLoad.SaveComplete is flags 0x12A: reg1 = _global, reg2 = successful.
movie SCRSAVELOAD
prepend-to function SaveComplete in ScrSaveLoad
    Push [reg2]
    Not
    If ssv_done
    GetURL 'FSCommand:SR_SaveEvent', 'save'
ssv_done:
end
